wasm32: a minor heap of 8M words (32 MB) by default.

The default of 256k words is 1 MB with 4-byte words, half the 2 MB of a
64-bit native program: programs allocating much spent their time in minor
collections.  Compiled, under node 26, from 1M to 8M words: binary_trees
1.40 s -> 0.86 s, hamming 0.27 s -> 0.18 s, boyer_no_exc 0.51 s -> 0.38 s,
gc_major 2.7 s -> 2.2 s, about as large as the young generation V8 gives
JavaScript.  The memory is only touched as the program allocates (since
OCaml 5.1 the heaps come from malloc, not cleared): a program allocating
little uses no more.  wasm64 keeps 256k words of 8 bytes.  OCAMLRUNPARAM's
s= still sets it.

--- a/runtime/caml/config.h
+++ b/runtime/caml/config.h
@@
 /* Default size of the minor zone. (words)  */
+#ifdef __wasm32__
+#define Minor_heap_def 8388608
+#else
 #define Minor_heap_def 262144
+#endif
